    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "therapists just tell me to \"reframe\" things or \"look for the silver lining.\" but there is no silver lining here. it's just a massive deficit. if a business was losing money like this for 20 years, everyone would tell you to just close it down and stop the bleeding. why is life different? why am i supposed to just keep investing more into a bankrupt existence? it feels like the only logical way to stop the loss is to just exit the game entirely.",
